From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:22:07 +0000
Subject: pinctrl: equilibrium: bind the xRX500 pin controller

The Intel MIPS xRX500 (GRX350/GRX500) SoCs embed the same Equilibrium
pinmux/GPIO block as Lightning Mountain, but the vendor device trees
describe it with its own compatible string. AVM's 4.9 BSP binds its
copy of this very driver to "intel,pinctrl-xrx500"
(arch/mips/boot/dts/lantiq/xrx500.dtsi: pinctrl@c80000, physical
0x16c80000, 0x80000 window), so the string is the established
hardware-description name for this instance and is what the xRX500
device trees carry.

Add it to the match table and document it in the binding. The register
layout is identical, so no driver logic changes are needed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/intel,lgm-io.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/intel,lgm-io.yaml
index 1144ca2896e3..e09c55ea4251 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/intel,lgm-io.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/intel,lgm-io.yaml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/pinctrl/intel,lgm-io.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Intel Lightning Mountain SoC pinmux & GPIO controller
+title: Intel Lightning Mountain and xRX500 SoC pinmux & GPIO controller
 
 maintainers:
   - Rahul Tanwar <rahul.tanwar@linux.intel.com>
@@ -15,7 +15,9 @@ description: |
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: intel,lgm-io
+    enum:
+      - intel,lgm-io
+      - intel,pinctrl-xrx500
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-equilibrium.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-equilibrium.c
index ba1c867b7b89..b7c8752898f1 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-equilibrium.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-equilibrium.c
@@ -951,6 +951,7 @@ static int eqbr_pinctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id eqbr_pinctrl_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "intel,lgm-io" },
+	{ .compatible = "intel,pinctrl-xrx500" },
 	{}
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, eqbr_pinctrl_dt_match);
